<title>USA: MagneTek buys Hungarian motor manufacturer.</title>
<headline>MagneTek buys Hungarian motor manufacturer.</headline>
<dateline>NASHVILLE, Tenn. 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>MagneTek Inc said on Friday it bought an electric motor manufacturing business from the Hungarian government for an undisclosed sum of cash.</p>
<p>The business, located 70 kilometres (43 miles) southeast of Budapest, made and marketed fractional horsepower motors for commercial application, the company said.</p>
<p>MagneTek, which makes integrated electrical products, already had an integral-horsepower motor factory in Budapest.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
